gaIC(){return"Our manifesto"},
gaID(){return"\u2014 The search for purpose gives meaning to our lives.\n\n\u2014 Living on autopilot is not living; we choose to move through life with awareness.\n\n\u2014 Life is better shared.\n\n\u2014 Our circles \u2014family, friends\u2014 are the network that holds us up.\n\n\u2014 We all need help, and asking for it is an act of courage.\n\n\u2014 Not every day is a good day, and we need a strategy for the hard ones.\n\n\u2014 Being well with ourselves is the foundation for being well with others.\n\n\u2014 Knowing ourselves is where it all begins."},
gaIE(){return"Your North"},
gaIF(){return"Having a North doesn't guarantee that you'll live life the way you want \u2014 unexpected turns, detours and surprises will always show up.\n\nBut not having one guarantees you won't live it that way.\n\nYour North is the compass that brings you back to center when the path gets blurry. It's not a fixed destination: it's a direction you choose every day.\n\nDefining it means starting to take the wheel. Every step stops being random and starts pointing toward something that's yours.\n\nAt Metriotes we want that ten years from now you don't find yourself feeling that life slipped through your fingers, without having lived it the way you wanted."},
gaIA(){return"Metriotes"},
gaIB(){return"Metriotes comes from the Greek \u03bc\u03b5\u03c4\u03c1\u03b9\u03cc\u03c4\u03b7\u03c2: balance, the right measure.\n\nIt's not a romantic ideal or a lukewarm average. It's a choice: to live in balance, not in the extremes.\n\nAnd living in balance starts by looking at what usually stays invisible to the eye.\n\nThe behaviors we repeat without noticing. The emotions we feel without naming them. What triggers them \u2014 an hour, a person, a place, a thought.\n\nMetriotes exists to make conscious what you can't see today. So you stop reacting on autopilot and start choosing with clarity.\n\nBecause only when you see what you couldn't see before, can you decide how you want to live.\n\nLet's begin."},
gaHz(){return"Define your north"},
gaHB(){return"Estimated time: 5-10 min"},
gaHE(){return"Complete this exercise in a quiet place without distractions. Take your time to reflect on your answers."},
gaHx(){return"Choose up to 5 values that are essential to you."},
gaHQ(){return"These values will help you make decisions and live your life according to what's really important to you."},
gaHF(){return"Maximum 5 values allowed"},
gaHC(){return"How would you like to be remembered?"},
gaHD(){return"I would like to be remembered as..."},
gaHS(){return u.m},
gaHT(){return"Write here..."},
gaHH(){return u.P},
gaHI(){return"I would change..."},
gaHR(){return"What do you choose to be your north?"},
gaHG(){return"Your north is that phrase or conviction that gives you energy every day to get out of your comfort zone and overcome your barriers.\n\nIt's not a one-time goal that gets completed and ends. It's your way of living, the principles and values that accompany you throughout life.\n\nA goal answers 'what do I want to achieve?', while the north answers 'how do I want to live?'"},
